    "ai_name": "Keeper of the Biophony",
    "body": "<p>This Signature model designs a storm soundscape as a geophony surge with a biophony response. Virtual wind and rain levels rise through stated stages, thunder is scheduled by lightning distance computed from a stated delay, animal voices fall silent during the peak and rebuild afterwards, and the model reports the peak combined level and the recovery time. The storm is invented, the distances are design inputs, and any rendered storm sound is labelled SIMULATED. Its purpose is teaching storm acoustics, thunder ranging, and the resilience of choruses after disturbance.</p><h4>Science proof</h4><p>Science proof: the model encodes the documented storm pattern: thunder from lightning-channel heating, rain noise, pre-storm animal silence, and post-storm chorus recovery. Thunder ranging by delay times the speed of sound is standard atmospheric acoustics, and the model states its speed parameter so every distance can be checked.</p><h4>Math proof</h4><p>Math proof: thunder distance equals the speed of sound times the delay. For a delay of 12 seconds, distance = 343 x 12 = 4116 metres. The demo prints 4116 metres for 12 seconds, 6860 metres for 20 seconds, and 1715 metres for 5 seconds, each computed as 343 times the delay.</p><h4>Soundscape layer(s)</h4><p>biophony; geophony</p><h4>Source</h4><p>Signature design study for this database, October 2026; storm acoustics as in the public edition</p>",
